# Single-Module Architecture Rules

This project uses **single-module** Clean Architecture via **package** separation.
Base package: `com.mascill.healthtrack`.

## Stack (DevSpeak)

Default — do **not** add alternatives unless the user asks:

| Concern | Use |
|---|---|
| Auth + Postgres CRUD | supabase-kt (`auth-kt`, `postgrest-kt`) + Ktor engine |
| DTO JSON | `kotlinx.serialization` (`@Serializable`, `@SerialName`) |
| Chat SSE (Phase 2) | OkHttp in `NetworkModule` |
| Preferences | DataStore, name `healthtrack_prefs` |
| Local database | Room |

**Do not** add Retrofit or Moshi. `data/service/` is unused. DataStore and Room are both part of this app: prefs in DataStore, tables in Room.

SDK (`io.github.jan.supabase`) **only** in `data/` and `di/SupabaseModule`. Never in `domain/` or `presentation/`.

## Package Structure

```
app/src/main/kotlin/com/mascill/healthtrack/
├── data/
│   ├── datasource/
│   │   ├── local/               # DataStore prefs and Room DAO
│   │   └── remote/              # *RemoteDataSource (supabase-kt / SSE)
│   ├── mapper/
│   ├── model/
│   │   ├── entity/              # Room entities
│   │   ├── request/
│   │   └── response/            # @Serializable DTOs
│   └── repository/              # *RepositoryImpl
├── domain/
│   ├── model/
│   ├── repository/              # interfaces — no SDK
│   └── usecase/
├── presentation/
│   ├── common/component + model
│   ├── navigation/
│   ├── theme/
│   └── [feature]/
├── di/
│   ├── AppModule.kt
│   ├── DispatcherModule.kt
│   ├── NetworkModule.kt         # OkHttp (SSE)
│   ├── SupabaseModule.kt        # Auth + Postgrest
│   ├── RepositoryModule.kt
│   ├── DataStoreModule.kt       # healthtrack_prefs
│   └── DatabaseModule.kt        # Room
├── util/
├── App.kt
└── MainActivity.kt
```

## Layer Dependencies

```
presentation → domain → data
```

### ALLOWED
- `presentation` → `domain` (UseCases, repository interfaces, domain models)
- `data` → `domain`
- Any layer → `util`, `di`

### FORBIDDEN
- `domain` → `data` / `presentation`
- `data` → `presentation`
- `presentation` or `domain` importing `io.github.jan.supabase`

## Feature Package Structure

```
presentation/[feature]/
├── component/
├── model/                        # [Feature]UIState.kt
├── [Feature]Screen.kt
└── [Feature]ViewModel.kt
```

## Build Configuration

AGP 9 includes Kotlin — do not apply `org.jetbrains.kotlin.android`.
Pin versions from `gradle/libs.versions.toml` (Navigation 3, Compose BOM, supabase-kt BOM).
Use Navigation 3 (`NavDisplay` / `NavKey`), not Navigation Compose `NavHost`.

Add the Room plugin and DataStore. Do **not** add Retrofit or Moshi. Serialization plugin is required (NavKey + DTOs).

## Naming Conventions

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Domain model | `*` | `Profile` |
| Response | `*Response` | `ProfileResponse` |
| Request | `*Request` | `ProfileOnboardingRequest` |
| Remote data source | `*RemoteDataSource` | `ProfileRemoteDataSource` |
| Repository interface | `*Repository` | `ProfileRepository` |
| Repository impl | `*RepositoryImpl` | `ProfileRepositoryImpl` |
| UseCase | `*UseCase` | `CompleteOnboardingUseCase` |
| ViewModel | `*ViewModel` | `SignInViewModel` |
| Screen | `*Screen` | `SignInScreen` |
| UI State | `*UIState` | `SignInUIState` |

## Import Organization

```kotlin
// 1. Android/Androidx
import android.content.Context
import androidx.compose.runtime.Composable

// 2. Third-party (supabase only in data/ and di/)
import dagger.hilt.android.lifecycle.HiltViewModel
import io.github.jan.supabase.auth.Auth

// 3. Project - Domain
import com.mascill.healthtrack.domain.model.Profile
import com.mascill.healthtrack.domain.repository.ProfileRepository

// 4. Project - Data
import com.mascill.healthtrack.data.repository.ProfileRepositoryImpl

// 5. Project - Presentation
import com.mascill.healthtrack.presentation.home.HomeViewModel

// 6. Project - Utilities
import com.mascill.healthtrack.util.Constants
```
